          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            is canonically a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+monoidal+category"} cartesian closed monoidal category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{H}, \times)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \times
            ”. But if, in addition to this canonical product,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            is equipped with
            %em another
            (hence necessarily non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"}> cartesian
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
            ”, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{H}, \otimes)
            might be called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em monoidal topos
          %p
            If the extra monoidal structure is also
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
            = succeed "-" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/doubly+closed+monoidal+category"} doubly closed monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            (with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            a
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bunched+logic"} bunched logic
          %p
            Of course, a topos may carry more than one non-cartesian monoidal category structure, and in some of the interesting examples, the various monoidal structures will be interlinked in some way. A typical example is the phenomenon of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plethysm"} plethysm
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
          #ViaDayConvolution.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes)
              a small
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C}, Set]
              is naturally a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/doubly+closed+monoidal+category"} doubly closed monoidal
              topos with respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
              tensor product.
          %p
          #SliceToposOverAMonoidObject.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (slice topos over a monoid object)
              %br/
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G} \in \mathbf{H}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+topos"} slice topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi 𝔾
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbb{G}}
              inherits a non-cartesian monoidal structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes_G
              induced from the product structure on
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔾
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi χ
                                      %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi 𝔾
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ]
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝔾
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 2
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi χ
                                      %mn 2
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi 𝔾
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ×
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 2
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %msub
                                      %mi χ
                                      %mn 1
                                    %mo ,
                                    %msub
                                      %mi χ
                                      %mn 2
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi 𝔾
                              %mo ×
                              %mi 𝔾
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mo ⋅
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi 𝔾
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left[
                    \\array{
                    X_1
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\chi_1}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{G}
                    }
                    \\;\;
                    \\right]
                    \\otimes_{\mathbb{G}}
                    \\left[
                    \\array{
                    X_2
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\chi_2}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{G}
                    }
                    \\;\;
                    \\right]
                    \\;\;
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\;\;
                    \\left[
                    \\array{
                    X_1 \times X_2
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{(\chi_1, \chi_2)}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{G} \times \mathbb{G}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\cdot}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{G}
                    }
                    \\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\right]
                    \\,.
            %p
              Such monoidal toposes are always biclosed and appear as categories of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+action+functionals"} local action functionals
              in the context of
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+quantization"} motivic quantization
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              This Ex.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SliceToposOverAMonoidObject"}
              overlaps with the previous Ex.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ViaDayConvolution"}
              in the case where the given topos is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              and the small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+category"} discrete category
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and the two definitions of a monoidal structure agree up to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          #ClassifyingToposForTheoryOfObjects.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos+for+the+theory+of+objects"} classifying topos for the theory of objects
              – namely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [FinSet, Set]
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitary+monad"} finitary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctors"} endofunctors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi End
                      %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} End_f(Set)
              – is naturally a monoidal topos under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              of endofunctors. A standard textbook reference is (
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone D3.2
              ). The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
              over this monoidal category is discussed in (
              %a{:href => "#Garner13"}> Garner 13
              ).
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              There are several variations on the theme of the previous example
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassifyingToposForTheoryOfObjects"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
              on the “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ̲
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underline{\;\;\;\;\;}
              ” monoidal category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              generated by a single object, where the “blank” may be filled in with some structure-connoting adjective. In the previous example, we had that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet^{op}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
              generated by a single object, but the blank might be filled in with “symmetric” (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+category"} permutation category
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℙ
                      %mo =
                      %mi Core
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P} = Core(FinSet)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+category"} braid category
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔹
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{B}
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinInj"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Fin
                          %mi inj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fin_{inj}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injections"} injections
              between them), or “strict” (the discrete category
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi M
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = [M^{op}, Set]
              acquires a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
              structure, but more interestingly, we have an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \simeq \{E, E\}
            %p
              where the right side is the category of cocontinuous
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ̲
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underline{\;\;\;\;\;}
              monoidal endofunctors. By transferring the endofunctor composition across the equivalence,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              acquires another monoidal product structure. In the classical symmetric case, this goes under names like
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plethysm"} plethystic monoidal product
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategory"} generalized multicategory
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/operad#Conceptual"} operad – A detailed conceptual treatment
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              The category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
              is a topos (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              on the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+category"} tree category
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman-Vogt+tensor+product"} Boardman-Vogt tensor product
          .num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              In &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#Dolan11"}> Dolan 2011
              \&amp;rbrack; is indicated a category of “toric
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaves"} quasicoherent sheaves
          %p
          #TangentInfinityTopos.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Given an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-topos
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"}
                tangent
                = succeed "-topos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \mathbf{H}
              carries the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/external+tensor+product"} external
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
            %p
              Similarly, given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}
                stable
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              (or more generally a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal+locus"} Joyal locus
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒳
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Grpd
                          %mn ∞
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒳
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_{\mathcal{X} \in Grpd_\infty} Func(\mathcal{X}, \mathcal{A})
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Grpd"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Grpd
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grpd_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+stable+homotopy+theory"} parameterized
              = succeed "-objects" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-topos
              and) should carry the corresponding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/external+tensor+product"} external tensor product
